━━━ stdout
Check file names and recommended metadata

Catalogue hygiene: filename slugs and recommended metadata, not schema validation.
A missing optional field is a note: it never fails --strict, and prints with --verbose.

Usage: opentide lint [OPTIONS]

Options:
      --fix
          Apply safe filename renames

      --strict
          Exit non-zero when errors or warnings are left (CI gate). Notes never fail it

      --check <CHECK>
          Limit to one check: filenames, metadata, recommended, placeholders or queries (repeatable). Runs it even when lint.toml disables it
          
          [possible values: filenames, metadata, recommended, placeholders, queries]

      --changed
          Lint only the object files this run changed: the pull or merge request, the push, or outside CI the last commit (the diff deploy reads)

      --file <FILE>
          Lint only this object file (repeatable)

      --format <REPORT_FORMAT>
          text: code frames. sarif: SARIF 2.1.0 for code scanning. codequality: GitLab Code Quality (Code Climate JSON). A report goes to --output, or to stdout instead of the text
          
          [default: text]
          [possible values: text, sarif, codequality]

      --output <OUTPUT>
          Write the --format report to this file and print the usual text output too

      --help
          Print help

Examples:
  $ opentide lint
  $ opentide lint --fix

━━━ stderr · empty
